m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Glutamate\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This synthesis network constructs glutamate from C1, C2, and C3 prebiotic precursors via a variety of justified routes, including hydrothermal reductive amination of \u03b1-ketoglutarate, surface-catalyzed transaminations, Strecker-type reactions, and hydrothermal CO2 fixation pathways. All molecules and reactions are stoichiometrically and structurally consistent, and each reaction conserves mass and charge. Multiple plausible hydrothermal and surface environments are leveraged, and alternative substrate choices are provided where justified by prebiotic chemistry. Every chemical step invokes only transformations with firm or strong experimental precedent; speculative steps are clearly marked and justified. Ten distinct pathways to glutamate are mapped, taking care not to introduce arbitrary connectivity or unnecessary intermediates.\n\nMOLECULES (17 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_003: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_004: C2H4O2 (acetic acid) [starting]\n  - mol_005: C3H6O3 (lactic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_006: C4H6O5 (\u03b1-ketoglutaric acid) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: C2H5NO2 (glycine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C3H7NO2 (alanine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C5H9NO4 (glutamic acid) [target]\n  - mol_010: C5H10N2O3 (glutamine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C5H8O3 (glutaric anhydride) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_013: C5H8N2O4 (glutamate Strecker intermediate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: NH4+ (ammonium ion) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: H2O (water) [intermediate]\n  - mol_016: C5H8O4 (glutaric acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_017: C4H7NO2 (aminobutyric acid) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (15 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_016, mol_001 -> mol_006 (Hydrothermal carboxylation of succinic acid to \u03b1-ketoglutarate) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_006, mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_009, mol_015 (Hydrothermal reductive amination of \u03b1-ketoglutarate to glutamate) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_003: mol_016, mol_012, mol_002, mol_015 -> mol_013 (Surface Strecker synthesis of glutamate from glutaric aldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_013, mol_015 -> mol_009, mol_012 (Hydrolysis of Strecker intermediate to glutamate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_011, mol_015 -> mol_016 (Hydration of glutaric anhydride to glutaric acid) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_006, mol_008 -> mol_009, mol_007 (Transamination between \u03b1-ketoglutarate and alanine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_007: mol_004, mol_012, mol_002, mol_015 -> mol_008 (Surface Strecker synthesis of alanine from pyruvate) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_005, mol_002 -> mol_008, mol_015 (Hydrothermal conversion of lactic acid to alanine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_009: mol_006, mol_002 -> mol_009 (Direct hydrothermal amination of \u03b1-ketoglutarate to glutamate) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_010: mol_006, mol_007 -> mol_009, mol_016 (Transamination between \u03b1-ketoglutarate and glycine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_011: mol_016, mol_002 -> mol_017, mol_015 (Amination of glutaric acid to aminobutyric acid) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_012: mol_017, mol_001 -> mol_009 (Carboxylation of aminobutyric acid to glutamate) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_013: mol_009, mol_002 -> mol_010 (Amidation of glutamate to glutamine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_014: mol_010, mol_015 -> mol_009, mol_014 (Hydrolysis of glutamine to glutamate and ammonium) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_015: mol_004, mol_012, mol_002, mol_015 -> mol_007 (Surface Strecker synthesis of glycine) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Classic Reductive Amination of \u03b1-Ketoglutarate (3 steps)\n  - P2: Strecker Synthesis on Surface-Mineral Phases (3 steps)\n  - P3: Transamination via Alanine (4 steps)\n  - P4: Alanine from Lactic Acid Pathway (4 steps)\n  - P5: Direct Non-reductive Amination (3 steps)\n  - P6: Transamination via Glycine (4 steps)\n  - P7: Glutaric Acid Reductive Amination and Carboxylation (3 steps)\n  - P8: Amidation and Hydrolysis via Glutamine (5 steps)\n  - P9: Parallel Reductive Amination and Surface/Aqueous Cycling (4 steps)\n  - P10: Dual Precursor Strecker/Transamination (6 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 15 reactions | 1 balanced as written | 2 balanceable with coefficients | 12 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: C5H8O4 + CO2 -> C4H6O5 | reactants minus products: C+2, H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as reactant; H2 as reactant; CO as product; O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_002 balanceable: 5 C4H6O5 + 4 NH3 + 6 H2 -> 4 C5H9NO4 + 9 H2O\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: C5H8O4 + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C5H8N2O4 | reactants minus products: C+1, H+6, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: C5H8N2O4 + H2O -> C5H9NO4 + HCN | reactants minus products: C-1, O+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: C5H8O3 + H2O -> C5H8O4 | reactants minus products: H+2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: C4H6O5 + C3H7NO2 -> C5H9NO4 + C2H5NO2 | reactants minus products: H-1, N-1, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; CO as reactant; HCN as reactant\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: C2H4O2 + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C3H7NO2 | reactants minus products: H+3, N+1, O+1 | balanceable if adding: CO2 as product; O2 as product\n  - rxn_009 UNBALANCED: C4H6O5 + NH3 -> C5H9NO4 | reactants minus products: C-1, O+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_010 UNBALANCED: C4H6O5 + C2H5NO2 -> C5H9NO4 + C5H8O4 | reactants minus products: C-4, H-6, O-1 | balanceable if adding: O2 as product\n  - rxn_011 balanceable: 4 C5H8O4 + 5 NH3 -> 5 C4H7NO2 + 6 H2O\n  - rxn_012 UNBALANCED: C4H7NO2 + CO2 -> C5H9NO4 | reactants minus products: H-2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant\n  - rxn_013 UNBALANCED: C5H9NO4 + NH3 -> C5H10N2O3 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_014 UNBALANCED: C5H10N2O3 + H2O -> C5H9NO4 + NH4+ | reactants minus products: H-1, charge -1 | balanceable if adding: H+ as reactant\n  - rxn_015 UNBALANCED: C2H4O2 + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C2H5NO2 | reactants minus products: C+1, H+5, N+1, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\nFormula/structure inconsistencies:\n  - mol_006: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_010: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_011: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_013: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_017: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\nTreat this check as ground truth for mass and charge conservation. Reactions that cannot be balanced violate conservation: reflect this in chemical_feasibility and reaction_scores, list them in problematic_reactions, and name the specific reaction IDs (with the missing species, if hinted) in your feedback so the network can be corrected. Note that implausibly large inferred coefficients may also indicate a mis-specified reaction.\n=== END BALANCE CHECK ===\n\n\nPlease evaluate the network and respond with JSON:\n{\n    \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"<id>\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\"rxn_001\": 0.85, ...},\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"environmental_progression\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"target_achievement\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"feedback\": \"<pathway-specific feedback>\",\n            \"approved\": <true if confidence >= 0.8>,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_ids with issues\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\"improvements\"]\n        }\n    ],\n    \"best_pathway_id\": \"<id of best pathway>\",\n    \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n    \"network_feedback\": \"<overall assessment>\"\n}\n\nNote: \"environmental_progression\" scores Environmental Consistency (conditions fit each\nreaction's stated environment), not any particular order of environments.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.6,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.6\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.7,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.85,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.95,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.95,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"feedback\": \"This pathway utilizes classic hydrothermal routes that have experimental precedent. rxn_002 is nearly balanced, but rxn_001 and rxn_009 are unbalanced, violating strict mass conservation. Some species appear to be missing (e.g., H2O). Mechanistically, steps are plausible and fit environmental constraint